#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133895 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133711 :question/id #uuid "a817c3c6-97bb-55e4-9a1e-04ed99d3eaab" :question/math-academy-id "e-9553" :question/problem "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve. Given that the line integral\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\oint\\limits_C \\mathbf{F} \\cdot \\text{d}\\mathbf{r}\n$$\n\n \nrepresents the area of the region $D$ enclosed by any such curve in $\\mathbb{R}^2,$ which of the following could be the vector field $\\mathbf{F}(x,y)?$\n\nI. $\\left\\langle -y, \\: y\\right\\rangle$\n\nII. $\\left\\langle -2x, \\: 2x\\right\\rangle$\n\nIII. $\\left\\langle 5y\\sin x, \\: x-5\\cos x \\right\\rangle$" :question/worked-solution "According to Green's theorem, if $\\mathbf{F}(x,y) = \\left\\langle P(x,y), \\: Q(x,y) \\right\\rangle,$ where\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x} - \\dfrac{\\partial P}{\\partial y} = 1,\n$$\n\nwe can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each pair in turn.\n\n- Vector field I gives the required area. In this case, \n$\\dfrac{\\partial P}{\\partial y} = -1$\nand\n$\\dfrac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x} = 0,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x} - \\dfrac{\\partial P}{\\partial y} = 1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field II does not give the required area. In this case, \n$\\dfrac{\\partial P}{\\partial y} = 0$\nand\n$\\dfrac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x} = 2,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x} - \\dfrac{\\partial P}{\\partial y} = 2.\n$$\n\n- Vector field III gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\dfrac{\\partial P}{\\partial y} = 5\\sin x$\nand\n$\\dfrac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x} = 1+5\\sin x,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x} - \\dfrac{\\partial P}{\\partial y} = 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5f4f726e-d985-5915-a4d0-30cfa6f4b89b" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134092 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99862250-7069-52b8-961c-43b2d6c3e458" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130709} {:answer/id #uuid "f68109da-5447-5289-9116-b22d249e0b40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130710} {:answer/id #uuid "5b193744-a5b0-5a56-a6c4-959a94a39569" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130711} {:answer/id #uuid "6b57aff0-91a2-5924-b717-b77009c0d3d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130712} {:answer/id #uuid "7be44107-414a-5573-bb82-9924ad37ebda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130713}] :answer-field/id #uuid "5d17d2d8-9928-5246-af09-a8de679c2edf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130708} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4bbde3ea-51a4-5bb9-b415-15b081645f8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369320} {:answer/id #uuid "7503552f-1a3f-5846-a2bb-20c103b29664" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369321} {:answer/id #uuid "8bb7ee7a-6e0f-5758-a561-9b3915b9f2e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369322} {:answer/id #uuid "17bae066-3d20-59d8-b46d-cf1882d28b09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369323} {:answer/id #uuid "902e9dbe-6cff-5089-8658-727ffe921b4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369324}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8bb7ee7a-6e0f-5758-a561-9b3915b9f2e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369322} :answer-field/id #uuid "633e4ab2-3db4-5baf-9514-75709128a17a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369319}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9d72f3f4-6ff1-53f9-94a6-72b405d3f343" :question/math-academy-id "q-125852" :question/problem "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve. Given that the line integral\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\n$$\n\n \nrepresents the area of the region $D$ enclosed by any such curve in ${R}^{2},$ which of the following could be the functions $P(x,y)$ and $Q(x,y)?$\n\n- $P(x,y)=y$ and $Q(x,y)=-x$\n- $P(x,y)=\\frac{x}{2}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{y}^{2}$ and $Q(x,y)=\\frac{y}{2}$\n- $P(x,y)=0$ and $Q(x,y)=x$" :question/worked-solution "According to Green's theorem, if \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1,\n$$\n\nwe can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each pair in turn.\n\n- Pair I does *not* give the required area. In this case, \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=-1,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-2\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Pair II does *not* give the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{2}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=0,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=2y\\operatorname{sin}⁡{y}^{2}\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Pair III gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=1,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134093 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "acef05c6-00e1-5592-a1a0-889b8fae112b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130715} {:answer/id #uuid "b7bd9e64-696c-51f2-9326-b4dd35e8d309" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130716} {:answer/id #uuid "033fba2e-49ef-5a43-86ee-97280d5189b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130717} {:answer/id #uuid "06170a0b-5016-5c98-abd7-afe22178d627" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130718} {:answer/id #uuid "4abc258a-2852-54fd-89be-f1ca43962d66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130719}] :answer-field/id #uuid "097d24ae-bf47-5570-8b59-107607077491" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186130714} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51032152-ac1c-5645-b519-4d9f91f449cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369326} {:answer/id #uuid "d548dfcc-afb7-5f57-ad90-cfdfdb29a3ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369327} {:answer/id #uuid "0cc64ba0-9932-5ec8-a8c1-902a58b2e272" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369328} {:answer/id #uuid "8c7ad01a-0f7e-5e8c-8299-0aee289f43aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369329} {:answer/id #uuid "9cfcd43c-0ace-5687-91b7-d1a23321bac2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369330}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51032152-ac1c-5645-b519-4d9f91f449cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369326} :answer-field/id #uuid "07c5c5c2-3396-52cb-9fba-4aead4b7e49a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369325}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0916e138-1ac3-5dc1-b5d3-86d819d37c90" :question/math-academy-id "q-125853" :question/problem "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve. Given that the line integral\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\n$$\n\n \nrepresents the area of the region $D$ enclosed by any such curve in ${R}^{2},$ which of the following could be the vector field $F(x,y)?$\n\n- $F(x,y)=⟨-y,\\,{x}^{2}+x⟩$\n- $F(x,y)=⟨-\\frac{y}{4}+x,\\,\\frac{3x}{4}⟩$\n- $F(x,y)=⟨-y,\\,0⟩$" :question/worked-solution "According to Green's theorem, if $F(x,y)=⟨P(x,y),\\,Q(x,y)⟩,$ where\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1,\n$$\n\nwe can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each pair in turn.\n\n- Vector field I does *not* give the required area. In this case, \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-1$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=2x+1,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=2x+2\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field II gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-\\frac{1}{4}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{3}{4},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field III gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-1$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=0,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369359 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1815869f-1306-5a7a-8a79-31aa7c3aed98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369361} {:answer/id #uuid "58993782-e81d-561a-8c2f-a709856b5298" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369362} {:answer/id #uuid "6c9bdb63-1c2c-5b12-a095-b34893ce6ab0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369363} {:answer/id #uuid "9cdced70-20f6-5c17-a5c6-34b0325d1ebf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369364} {:answer/id #uuid "e393d19c-d776-50ae-81aa-fc2b967ef5f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369365}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58993782-e81d-561a-8c2f-a709856b5298" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369362} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a1e341d-7570-5f89-bb15-0d2fc13ee8fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369360}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cf5aefc1-27f1-5c4b-be31-6e2e9699a7da" :question/math-academy-id "q-126560" :question/problem "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve. Given that the line integral\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\n$$\n\n \nrepresents the area of the region $D$ enclosed by any such curve in ${R}^{2},$ which of the following could be the functions $P(x,y)$ and $Q(x,y)?$\n\n- $P(x,y)={e}^{x+y}-\\frac{y}{2}$ and $Q(x,y)={e}^{x+y}+\\frac{x}{2}$\n- $P(x,y)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y$ and $Q(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$\n- $P(x,y)=x$ and $Q(x,y)=x$" :question/worked-solution "According to Green's theorem, if \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1,\n$$\n\nwe can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each pair in turn.\n\n- Pair I gives the required area.  In this case,\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}={e}^{x+y}-\\frac{1}{2}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}={e}^{x+y}+\\frac{1}{2},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\n- Pair II does *not* give the required area.  Notice that \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Pair III gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=1,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369366 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0df9c250-7ee0-5ece-be23-b462fd5a422f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369368} {:answer/id #uuid "06a0083a-8cd7-5f98-9890-958e33d75b4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369369} {:answer/id #uuid "b520c185-893f-5860-8fa0-f1bb18583ae8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369370} {:answer/id #uuid "b812902c-4800-53c3-8754-8db8226bf6aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369371} {:answer/id #uuid "b3254e94-deb8-5a0b-aec5-298a58eed547" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369372}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06a0083a-8cd7-5f98-9890-958e33d75b4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369369} :answer-field/id #uuid "9dea12d4-5756-5452-8729-3752e57f331e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369367}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5decc408-adb2-55a3-accb-8195735690a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-126571" :question/problem "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve. Given that the line integral\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\n$$\n\n \nrepresents the area of the region $D$ enclosed by any such curve in ${R}^{2},$ which of the following could be the vector field $F(x,y)?$\n\n- $F(x,y)=⟨0,\\,x⟩$\n- $F(x,y)=⟨{e}^{y},\\,y⟩$\n- $F(x,y)=⟨-\\frac{y}{5}+\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,\\,\\frac{4x}{5}⟩$" :question/worked-solution "According to Green's theorem, if $F(x,y)=⟨P(x,y),\\,Q(x,y)⟩,$ where\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1,\n$$\n\nwe can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each pair in turn.\n\n- Vector field I give the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=1,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\n- Pair II does *not* give the required area. In this case, \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}={e}^{y}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=0,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-{e}^{y}\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Pair III gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-\\frac{1}{5}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{4}{5},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369373 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1682494d-d524-5563-b569-856dbdf7297a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369375} {:answer/id #uuid "e3d4788d-f0bc-5750-a40b-058b24c090d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369376} {:answer/id #uuid "611ef7e9-ee73-5906-a42c-5c6fb21ca78b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369377} {:answer/id #uuid "77c2f880-1ea2-53a0-b72f-16fd1455fdbf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369378} {:answer/id #uuid "e414b1b8-edc6-5c45-a972-64d39ae18795" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369379}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "611ef7e9-ee73-5906-a42c-5c6fb21ca78b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369377} :answer-field/id #uuid "e30dc9f1-8788-5cd6-85f2-29a70154514e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369374}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a19e15dc-6544-52f9-9d54-2c5e5b2885d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-126577" :question/problem "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve. Given that the line integral\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\n$$\n\n \nrepresents the area of the region $D$ enclosed by any such curve in ${R}^{2},$ which of the following could be the vector field $F(x,y)?$\n\n- $F(x,y)=⟨y,\\,y⟩$\n- $F(x,y)=⟨\\frac{y}{7},\\,\\frac{6x}{7}⟩$\n- $F(x,y)=⟨{e}^{x}-{e}^{-y},\\,x{e}^{-y}+x⟩$" :question/worked-solution "According to Green's theorem, if $F(x,y)=⟨P(x,y),\\,Q(x,y)⟩,$ where\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1,\n$$\n\nwe can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each pair in turn.\n\n- Vector field I does *not* give the required area. In this case, \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=0,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-1\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field II does *not* give the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{1}{7}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{6}{7},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{5}{7}\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field III gives the required area.  Notice that \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}={e}^{-y}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}={e}^{-y}+1,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431048 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f503e12-e11c-54c7-8ba7-5830ef6f73bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431014} {:answer/id #uuid "20a55ace-f5e1-5a5a-91ce-2c0b7d1404a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431015} {:answer/id #uuid "4798dafc-c73d-5ec4-b12f-da6f6620e4dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431022} {:answer/id #uuid "8a583e9f-a399-590a-ac83-6aef2ccb73c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431030} {:answer/id #uuid "fac08602-5de8-5d47-96f6-859f484e607d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431040}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4798dafc-c73d-5ec4-b12f-da6f6620e4dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431022} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3715f35-6d8a-57c2-a089-fd1bb9bddf47" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431046}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1d67db6a-7337-599e-8ecc-26284642ae3b" :question/math-academy-id "q-126574" :question/problem "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve. Given that the line integral\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\n$$\n\n \nrepresents the area of the region $D$ enclosed by any such curve in ${R}^{2},$ which of the following could be the vector field $F(x,y)?$\n\nI. $F(x,y)=⟨y{e}^{x},\\,x-{e}^{x}⟩$\n\nII. $F(x,y)=⟨2y,\\,x⟩$\n\nIII. $F(x,y)=⟨-\\frac{y}{3}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{x}^{2},\\,\\frac{2x}{3}+1⟩$" :question/worked-solution "According to Green's theorem, if $F(x,y)=⟨P(x,y),\\,Q(x,y)⟩,$ where\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1,\n$$\n\nwe can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each pair in turn.\n\n- Vector field I does *not* give the required area. In this case, \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}={e}^{x}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=1-{e}^{x},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1-2{e}^{x}\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field II does *not* give the required area. Notice that \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=2$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=1,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-1\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field III gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=-\\frac{1}{3}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{2}{3},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186431050 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0de6da70-c426-566d-b3d0-dce7471f5600" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431013} {:answer/id #uuid "576c0bfb-effc-5ce5-827d-af6530c65e4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431025} {:answer/id #uuid "a5d96a71-7dc4-568f-af4e-fef495f9c448" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431033} {:answer/id #uuid "cd786957-3ffe-55c0-a40e-e21f738990d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431035} {:answer/id #uuid "fcb13b39-dc15-5bed-8347-e772308dd574" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431041}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "576c0bfb-effc-5ce5-827d-af6530c65e4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431025} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd054105-4a4d-5e12-a937-81dcca4212b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186431047}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2c0dea55-217c-592d-9a6c-d305c8e67729" :question/math-academy-id "q-126575" :question/problem "Let $C$ be a simple, piecewise-smooth, closed, and positively oriented curve. Given that the line integral\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\n$$\n\n \nrepresents the area of the region $D$ enclosed by any such curve in ${R}^{2},$ which of the following could be the vector field $F(x,y)?$\n\nI. $F(x,y)=⟨{y}^{3},\\,{x}^{3}+1⟩$\n\nII. $F(x,y)=⟨\\frac{y}{2}+\\sqrt{2}x,\\,\\frac{3x}{2}⟩$\n\nIII. $F(x,y)=⟨x,\\,x⟩$" :question/worked-solution "According to Green's theorem, if $F(x,y)=⟨P(x,y),\\,Q(x,y)⟩,$ where\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1,\n$$\n\nwe can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each pair in turn.\n\n- Vector field I does *not* give the required area. In this case, \n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=3{y}^{2}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=3{x}^{2},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=3{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2}\\ne 1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field II gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{1}{2}$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{3}{2},$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\n- Vector field III gives the required area. Notice that\n$\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0$\nand\n$\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=1,$\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields That Satisfy the Unit Curl Property"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133896 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133712 :question/id #uuid "74c9ecfb-5005-53ff-b7a9-db798488587b" :question/math-academy-id "e-9554" :question/problem "Let $D$ be the region enclosed by the curve $C$ parametrized as\n$\\mathbf{r}(t) = \\langle 2\\sin t, \\: 2 \\cos t \\rangle$ for $t \\in \\left [0, 2\\pi \\right).$ \nThe area of $D$ can be written as\n\n![](images/45/45513e4aedd37b868d2020cbbb47f49938f6ca03487ded8b5e519a2ec8e4edf5.svg)\n\nwhere $P(x,y) = -y$ and $Q(x,y) = 0.$ Determine the missing part of the equation.\n\n*Hint: Note that $C$ is negatively oriented.*\n\n![](images/a5/a5eeb5db90f9ee0d86a49e5bbf02629c7886fa019db7cff3c4d0e1eb43e8fd75.png)" :question/worked-solution "Our simple, smooth, closed path $C$ is negatively oriented, and  \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\partial Q}{\\partial x} - \\dfrac{\\partial P}{\\partial y} = 0 - \\left(-1\\right) = 1.\n$$\n\nSo, according to Green's theorem, we can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nNotice that we have to take the line integral with a minus sign since the path is negatively oriented.\n\nSubstituting $P(x,y) = -y$ and $Q(x,y) = 0,$ we get\n\n$$\n- \\oint\\limits_C P \\: \\text{d}x + Q \\: \\text{d}y = \\oint\\limits_C y \\: \\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe derivative of $\\mathbf r(t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}'(t) = \\left\\langle  2\\cos t ,\\:  -2 \\sin t \\right\\rangle.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }4{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $4\\cos^2 t.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8644454b-ee25-59fd-ae65-9770a0b44442" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134377 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9889fb55-466c-599c-9bd9-39de83c495a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos te^{\\cos t + \\sin t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132302} {:answer/id #uuid "c8c76777-0d91-5baf-97bc-f361e8108b96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos te^{\\cos t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132303} {:answer/id #uuid "cfe42eb5-9854-582d-9859-5abe648bfbf4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin te^{\\cos t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132304} {:answer/id #uuid "d67786d5-6f74-5303-a34c-74f8042bfccb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sin te^{\\sin t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132305} {:answer/id #uuid "f9017218-f44b-5874-b5f4-765f34a654ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sin te^{\\cos t + \\sin t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132306}] :answer-field/id #uuid "0f782c02-0bd7-576d-a703-443eb8f872fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132301}] :question/id #uuid "097af826-94c0-5b59-ad65-7d59555aa9e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-42221" :question/problem "![](images/44/4408d1fcee1d168c6ab21ea53cf24845093bad9cc608299a36f0510c1636cc03.png)\n\nLet $D$ be the region enclosed by the curve $C$ parametrized as\n$r(t) = ⟨e^{\\cos t}, e^{\\sin t}⟩$ for $t ∈ [0, 2π]$. The area of $D$ can be written as\n\n$Area(D) = ∬_(D)(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x} - \\frac{∂P}{∂y})dA = \\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{2π}AAAAAAAdt$,\n\nwhere $P(x, y) = 0$ and $Q(x, y) = x$. Determine the missing part of the equation."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134378 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b99d9fa-8746-5b24-b150-3778d2789fbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\cos^{2} t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132308} {:answer/id #uuid "4f557510-890d-5c72-baca-50a8aed5cc6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\sin^{2} t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132309} {:answer/id #uuid "656aa773-8708-58ce-aa12-99b62f7bf252" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\cos^{2} t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132310} {:answer/id #uuid "66e986c0-94a1-5f87-83fb-83d5fe3f5305" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\sin t\\cos t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132311} {:answer/id #uuid "6dca153e-7fc2-5baf-9c77-fca9326e5002" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sin t\\cos t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132312}] :answer-field/id #uuid "ff01fd58-b994-5d7c-8628-db2542bb8485" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132307} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9daf741d-ed1d-5418-9a08-c962cd04f234" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6{sin}^{2}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392496} {:answer/id #uuid "29dfbde4-ae70-5670-a1c3-f06b16942b59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392497} {:answer/id #uuid "3efa1f4b-972e-5984-9ba9-47ae745edcc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6{cos}^{2}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392498} {:answer/id #uuid "607a8eb7-ea64-55b5-903c-5325b01df2c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392499} {:answer/id #uuid "de2df677-04a7-58a1-b729-58fb2faf6e9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{cos}^{2}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392500}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "de2df677-04a7-58a1-b729-58fb2faf6e9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{cos}^{2}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392500} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba482bd4-ad69-5775-80d8-0a8566f264c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392495}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "321757db-d917-5b82-a83a-32bb4ce151f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-42238" :question/problem "![](images/6f/6f51a25843259881994e3dca0781b780878bec349930b76fbf449dc824e69ec2.png)\n\nLet $D$ be the region enclosed by the curve $C$ parametrized as\n$r(t)=⟨2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ].$ \nThe area of $D$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})dA={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\boxed{}\\,dt,\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x,y)=-y$ and $Q(x,y)=0.$ Determine the missing part of the equation.\n\n*Hint: Note that $C$ is negatively oriented.*" :question/worked-solution "Our simple, smooth, closed path $C$ is negatively oriented, and  \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0-(-1)=1.\n$$\n\nSo, according to Green's theorem, we can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nNotice that we have to take the line integral with a minus sign since the path is negatively oriented.\n\nSubstituting $P(x,y)=-y$ and $Q(x,y)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n-{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y={∮}_{C}y\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is\n\n$$\n{r}^{′}(t)=⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }6{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369413 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "396b8bd9-301b-51ec-aca0-06cdba5ad003" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369415} {:answer/id #uuid "a8dbb119-5910-5170-9d33-e634a7d5b88b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369416} {:answer/id #uuid "d7ec21fa-558f-57a8-81bd-b660d625d1a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{e}^{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369417} {:answer/id #uuid "1a2f5977-a0c7-5e88-b88d-158811b0198d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369418} {:answer/id #uuid "f3580aca-f980-54b4-b266-0dffc5f943b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369419}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8dbb119-5910-5170-9d33-e634a7d5b88b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369416} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff67740a-3837-5c9c-8e44-2824507f3d72" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369414}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e9ca0a08-e6bb-50c4-bb79-c63c0eceed7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-126750" :question/problem "![](images/0d/0d988bfd18a945ba96c3556775d4aebc706252e2baf02d5f76c108e5534baed1.png)\n\nLet $D$ be the region enclosed by the curve $C$ parametrized as\n$r(t)=⟨{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t},\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}⟩$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ].$ \nThe area of $D$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})dA={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\boxed{}\\,dt,\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x,y)=-y$ and $Q(x,y)=0.$ Determine the missing part of the equation.\n\n*Hint: Note that $C$ is negatively oriented.*" :question/worked-solution "Our simple, smooth, closed path $C$ is negatively oriented, and  \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=0-(-1)=1.\n$$\n\nSo, according to Green's theorem, we can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nNotice that we have to take the line integral with a minus sign since the path is negatively oriented.\n\nSubstituting $P(x,y)=-y$ and $Q(x,y)=0,$ we get\n\n$$\n-{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y={∮}_{C}y\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is\n\n$$\n{r}^{′}(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t},\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369420 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f0d281b3-5a65-5abd-9147-9fa81d7479a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369422} {:answer/id #uuid "771eb8e2-5fd8-5c34-9cab-6baf30556342" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369423} {:answer/id #uuid "1186811b-cecf-5cd1-866d-f83bda30e6d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369424} {:answer/id #uuid "26818ab1-0eaf-5fec-bae5-cdb88bcda5c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369425} {:answer/id #uuid "af5ef701-94c2-5be2-ab98-f0bb5078f369" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369426}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "771eb8e2-5fd8-5c34-9cab-6baf30556342" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369423} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0b9dd1e-629f-5bde-86fc-a981f5b5dd34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369421}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5399a5fd-5cdb-5780-b3c9-dad2d4175154" :question/math-academy-id "q-126751" :question/problem "![](images/81/81da86ae54a837b954bf93f8a75d93e1e7a8b64c93ba6f6b06cf74b2d8fa7ecb.png)\n\nLet $D$ be the region enclosed by the curve $C$ parametrized as\n$r(t)=⟨2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t⟩$ for $t\\in [0,\\pi ].$ \nThe area of $D$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})dA={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\boxed{}\\,dt,\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x,y)=0$ and $Q(x,y)=x.$ Determine the missing part of the equation.\n\n*Hint: Note that $C$ is negatively oriented.*" :question/worked-solution "Our simple, smooth, closed path $C$ is negatively oriented, and  \n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=1-0=1.\n$$\n\nSo, according to Green's theorem, we can write the area of the region $D$ enclosed by the curve $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(D) & ={∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}-\\frac{∂P}{∂y})\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nNotice that we have to take the line integral with a minus sign since the path is negatively oriented.\n\nSubstituting $P(x,y)=0$ and $Q(x,y)=x,$ we get\n\n$$\n-{∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y={∮}_{C}-x\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe derivative of $r(t)$ is\n\n$$\n{r}^{′}(t)=⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write our line integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}-x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\cdot 6\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,dt \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370913 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2af7955-e8f7-5d06-9494-41b60d32dda6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370915} {:answer/id #uuid "eeb61e07-30d9-5656-b689-8f8a3ed177fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6({sin}^{2}⁡t-{cos}^{2}⁡t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370916} {:answer/id #uuid "08be8790-c0ff-5547-af1e-b5707ffe8884" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6({cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370917} {:answer/id #uuid "050b2982-51ab-5396-940b-7dbb8bae2852" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{sin}^{2}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 1759