lockwise and ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ are oriented clockwise, calculate the value of ${∮}_{∂D}F\\cdot \\text{d}r.$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the total circulation of a vector field over the boundary of a region containing holes, we add together the circulations over each *positively oriented* boundary.\n\nRemember that:\n\n- the positive direction is *counterclockwise* for the *outer* curve ${C}_{1}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{1}$ counterclockwise), and\n\n- the positive direction is *clockwise* for the *inner* curves ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ (because the region $D$ is always on the left as we traverse ${C}_{2}$ and ${C}_{3}$ clockwise).\n\nThe diagram below shows the positive orientations of all three curves.\n\n![](images/52/527eb8572b90c3d2a4449b69015a9b94f4d121b094be6629e1b92c45f2ff0eb0.png)\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{∂D}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={∮}_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{∮}_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r+{∮}_{{C}_{3}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r \\\\  & =1+7+(-4) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186369476 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e510a18e-355c-5760-a4ed-c27a7d87f4e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369478} {:answer/id #uuid "57708075-d434-55d2-9a8f-50cf869df4aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369479} {:answer/id #uuid "ef5552ef-88b6-5aae-9816-a98a72f5bfb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369480} {:answer/id #uuid "e2e548cf-aab0-5f75-aa5e-55e9f6b0ab38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369481} {:answer/id #uuid "a2ba05f7-beee-5f04-830c-1ff34eb38cd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186369482}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2e548cf-aab0-5f75-aa5e-55e9f6b0ab38" :an